# DEFAULT-DENY, and the default is the point.
#
# This directory used to be `dev/epanet-models/`, which the root .gitignore excluded WHOLESALE
# because Tom drops real client water models in here to stress-test the .inp importer -- models
# carrying client names, real state-plane coordinates, base maps and fire-flow results, in a repo
# that is on GitHub.
#
# Renaming the directory to `dev/water-network-examples/` on 2026-08-14 silently removed that
# protection: the root rule named the old path, so the moment the folder changed name every client
# file in it became an ordinary untracked file that `git add dev/water-network-examples/` would
# publish. Nothing warned; the rename looked like a rename.
#
# So the protection lives INSIDE the directory now, where it travels with it, and it is a
# whitelist rather than a blacklist. A blacklist has to predict the next client file's name; a
# whitelist only has to know what we deliberately ship. When an example is ready to publish, add
# a line for it here -- that line IS the publication decision, and it is reviewable in the diff.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md

# The shipped examples (ROADMAP Task 314). Each of these is a saved project of ours, cleared for
# publication, and each is a file the examples gallery serves.
!Net1-lpn.json
!Net2-lpn.json
!Net3-lpn.json
!Elm-Street-Center-lpn.json
!descriptions.json
